s a past participle.","D":"Had cannot follow will directly."}}},{"id":"3d334470-c3c4-5a5f-acb7-51a6cb429693","topicSlug":"future-perfect-continuous","level":"B2","prompt":"Use future perfect continuous: By noon, I ____ the garden fence for two hours.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"will have been measuring"},{"id":"B","text":"will have being measuring"},{"id":"C","text":"will been measuring"},{"id":"D","text":"will have be measuring"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Combine the future auxiliary with **have been + -ing** to measure duration.","explanation":"The duration measured at noon is expressed by **will have been measuring**.","keywords":["future-duration"],"skill":"future-duration","contextKey":"future-perfect-continuous-3","fingerprint":"ac2435ca8fb8c6cbc5e630126e64714539a902253c31a55ea9a48bfc3cf3b8c6","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-future-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Combine the future auxiliary with **have been + -ing** to measure duration.","The duration measured at noon is expressed by **will have been measuring**.","Choose **will have been measuring**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The duration measured at noon is expressed by **will have been measuring**.","B":"Use the past participle been, not being, after have.","C":"Have is missing and will cannot take been directly.","D":"Have needs been, not base be."}}},{"id":"6ac4fbf1-5b8d-53bc-aaa2-f16fa21a2053","topicSlug":"future-perfect-continuous","level":"B2","prompt":"Choose the opening for a future-perfect question about the garden fence: ____ they have measured it by Friday?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Do"},{"id":"B","text":"Will have"},{"id":"C","text":"Will"},{"id":"D","text":"Have"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"In a multi-auxiliary question, move **only the first auxiliary**.","explanation":"Only **will** moves before the subject; have stays after they.","keywords":["future-question-order"],"skill":"future-question-order","contextKey":"future-perfect-continuous-3","fingerprint":"f0baf4826e7177ca26f639acb09ef184a366ea920c1b16879e0fbca2f8413147","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-future-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["In a multi-auxiliary question, move **only the first auxiliary**.","Only **will** moves before the subject; have stays after they.","Choose **Will**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Do is not added when will is the first auxiliary.","B":"This would repeat have and put two auxiliaries before the subject.","C":"Only **will** moves before the subject; have stays after they.","D":"The sentence already has have after they; the future auxiliary is missing."}}},{"id":"776074a6-72d8-5988-a02f-76fc289a0b99","topicSlug":"future-perfect-continuous","level":"B2","prompt":"Use future continuous: At ten tomorrow, we ____ the travel leaflet.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"will be translating"},{"id":"B","text":"will translating"},{"id":"C","text":"will been translating"},{"id":"D","text":"will be translated"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Picture the activity **in progress at a future time**.","explanation":"Future continuous pictures an activity at that moment: **will be translating**.","keywords":["future-in-progress"],"skill":"future-in-progress","contextKey":"future-perfect-continuous-4","fingerprint":"d057fa6ffa01358ba53cdfc1b2f9e17b0de7db9f25d3c9166a53a689e547619a","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-future-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Picture the activity **in progress at a future time**.","Future continuous pictures an activity at that moment: **will be translating**.","Choose **will be translating**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Future continuous pictures an activity at that moment: **will be translating**.","B":"Be is needed before the -ing form.","C":"After will use base be, not been.","D":"This is a passive-shaped phrase, not the requested active continuous."}}},{"id":"97ef5a50-cbd5-5f54-a865-adbf88ef7aeb","topicSlug":"future-perfect-continuous","level":"B2","prompt":"Use future perfect simple: By Friday, they ____ the travel leaflet.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"will has translated"},{"id":"B","text":"will have translating"},{"id":"C","text":"will had translated"},{"id":"D","text":"will have translated"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"By gives a future deadline. Build **will + have + participle**.","explanation":"The future perfect simple is **will have translated**, looking back from Friday.","keywords":["future-completion"],"skill":"future-completion","contextKey":"future-perfect-continuous-4","fingerprint":"faf2e6fbd8990a9e96fe013d406f3d1df93f14a8f943b0dfdcf5f1ed6e672726","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-future-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["By gives a future deadline. Build **will + have + participle**.","The future perfect simple is **will have translated**, looking back from Friday.","Choose **will have translated**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Have must remain base form after will.","B":"Perfect simple needs a past participle.","C":"Had cannot follow will directly.","D":"The future perfect simple is **will have translated**, looking back from Friday."}}},{"id":"a8a4ba3f-af17-584e-a306-0cc6d0bdc47d","topicSlug":"future-perfect-continuous","level":"B2","prompt":"Use future 